(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State the Rouche-Capelli Theorem governing the consistency of a non-homogeneous system AX = B, and provide a comprehensive theoretical proof.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement of Rouche-Capelli Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Consider a system of m linear algebraic equations in n unknowns: AX = B, where A in M_{m x) Tj
T*
(   n}\(R\), X in R^n, and B in R^m.) Tj
T*
(   Let [A | B] be the augmented matrix of order m x \(n+1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Condition 1 \(Consistency\): The system AX = B is consistent \(possesses at least one solution\)) Tj
T*
(   if and only if rank\(A\) = rank\([A | B]\).) Tj
T*
(   - Condition 2 \(Unique Solution\): If rank\(A\) = rank\([A | B]\) = n \(number of unknowns\), the) Tj
T*
(   system has a unique solution.) Tj
T*
(   - Condition 3 \(Infinite Solutions\): If rank\(A\) = rank\([A | B]\) = r < n, the system has) Tj
T*
(   infinitely many solutions parameterized by \(n - r\) independent free variables.) Tj
T*
(   - Condition 4 \(Inconsistency\): If rank\(A\) < rank\([A | B]\), the system is inconsistent \(no) Tj
T*
(   solution exists\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Theoretical Proof:) Tj
T*
(   - Let C1, C2, ..., Cn denote the column vectors of matrix A.) Tj
T*
(   - Then the matrix-vector product AX can be expanded as a linear combination of the columns of) Tj
T*
(   A:) Tj
T*
(   AX = x1*C1 + x2*C2 + ... + xn*Cn.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore, the system AX = B is solvable if and only if B can be expressed as:) Tj
T*
(   B = x1*C1 + x2*C2 + ... + xn*Cn.) Tj
T*
(   - This vector equation holds if and only if the vector B belongs to the column space \(range\) of) Tj
T*
(   A:) Tj
T*
(   B in Col\(A\) = Span{C1, C2, ..., Cn}.) Tj
T*
(   - If B in Col\(A\), then Span{C1, C2, ..., Cn, B} = Span{C1, C2, ..., Cn}.) Tj
T*
(   Taking dimensions: dim\(Span{C1, ..., Cn, B}\) = dim\(Span{C1, ..., Cn}\), which means:) Tj
T*
(   rank\([A | B]\) = rank\(A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Conversely, if B not in Col\(A\), then adding B increases the dimension of the spanned space by) Tj
T*
(   1:) Tj
T*
(   rank\([A | B]\) = rank\(A\) + 1 > rank\(A\). In this case, no scalars x1, ..., xn exist such that AX) Tj
T*
(   = B; hence, no solution exists.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
