(   - For unique vs infinite solutions: By the Rank-Nullity theorem, dim\(Null\(A\)\) = n - rank\(A\) = n) Tj
T*
(   - r.) Tj
T*
(   If r = n, Null\(A\) = {0}, giving a unique particular solution X = X_p.) Tj
T*
(   If r < n, general solution is X = X_p + X_h, where X_h spans an \(n - r\)-dimensional subspace,) Tj
T*
(   yielding infinitely many solutions. Hence proved.) Tj
