(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structure of Solution Space of AX = 0:) Tj
T*
(   - Let A in M_{m x n}\(R\). The set of all solutions to AX = 0 is defined as the Null Space) Tj
T*
(   \(Kernel\) of A:) Tj
T*
(   Null\(A\) = { X in R^n : AX = 0 }.) Tj
T*
(   - Null\(A\) is a subspace of R^n because:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Zero vector: A * 0 = 0 => 0 in Null\(A\).) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Additive closure: If X1, X2 in Null\(A\), then A\(X1 + X2\) = AX1 + AX2 = 0 + 0 = 0 => X1 + X2) Tj
T*
(   in Null\(A\).) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) Scalar closure: If X in Null\(A\) and c in R, then A\(c*X\) = c*\(AX\) = c*0 = 0 => c*X in) Tj
T*
(   Null\(A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Nullity of A is defined as the dimension of Null\(A\): nullity\(A\) = dim\(Null\(A\)\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Formal Statement of Rank-Nullity Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   For any m x n matrix A:) Tj
T*
(   rank\(A\) + nullity\(A\) = n \(the total number of columns / variables\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Mathematical Proof:) Tj
T*
(   - Reduce A to Reduced Row Echelon Form \(RREF\) R via elementary row operations.) Tj
T*
(   - Let rank\(A\) = r. Then R has exactly r non-zero rows, each containing a leading 1 \(pivot\).) Tj
T*
(   - The n variables x1, x2, ..., xn are partitioned into two disjoint subsets:) Tj
T*
(   * r Pivot \(Basic\) variables: corresponding to columns containing leading 1s.) Tj
T*
(   * \(n - r\) Free variables: corresponding to columns without leading 1s. Let these be t1, t2,) Tj
T*
(   ..., t_{n-r}.) Tj
T*
(   - Each basic variable can be uniquely expressed as a linear combination of the \(n - r\) free) Tj
T*
(   variables.) Tj
T*
(   - Setting one free variable to 1 and all others to 0 generates a solution vector V_j \(for j =) Tj
T*
(   1, 2, ..., n - r\).) Tj
T*
(   - These \(n - r\) vectors {V1, V2, ..., V_{n-r}} are linearly independent because in the free) Tj
T*
(   variable positions, they contain the columns of the \(n - r\) x \(n - r\) identity matrix.) Tj
T*
(   - Any solution X to AX = 0 is a linear combination of {V1, ..., V_{n-r}}:) Tj
T*
(   X = t1*V1 + t2*V2 + ... + t_{n-r}*V_{n-r}.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore, {V1, ..., V_{n-r}} forms a basis for Null\(A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Consequently, dim\(Null\(A\)\) = nullity\(A\) = n - r.) Tj
T*
(   - Since r = rank\(A\), we obtain: rank\(A\) + nullity\(A\) = r + \(n - r\) = n. Hence proved.) Tj
T*
