(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Gauss-Seidel iterative method for solving AX = B. State the sufficient condition for convergence \(diagonally dominant matrix\) and perform 3 iterations for the system: 8x - 3y + 2z = 20; 4x + 11y - z = 33; 6x + 3y + 12z = 35, starting from \(0, 0, 0\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Gauss-Seidel Method and Convergence Criterion:) Tj
T*
(   - For a system AX = B, write each variable x_i in terms of the remaining variables:) Tj
T*
(   x_i^\(k+1\) = \(1 / a_ii\) * [ b_i - sum_{j < i} a_ij * x_j^\(k+1\) - sum_{j > i} a_ij * x_j^\(k\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - The Gauss-Seidel method uses newly computed values x_j^\(k+1\) immediately in the current) Tj
T*
(   iteration.) Tj
T*
(   - Sufficient Condition for Convergence: The coefficient matrix A is strictly diagonally) Tj
T*
(   dominant:) Tj
T*
(   |a_ii| > sum_{j != i} |a_ij| for all i = 1, 2, ..., n.) Tj
T*
(   - Verification for given system:) Tj
T*
(   Row 1: |8| > |-3| + |2| = 5 \(True: 8 > 5\).) Tj
T*
(   Row 2: |11| > |4| + |-1| = 5 \(True: 11 > 5\).) Tj
T*
(   Row 3: |12| > |6| + |3| = 9 \(True: 12 > 9\).) Tj
T*
(   The system is strictly diagonally dominant, guaranteeing rapid convergence.) Tj
T*
(   2. Iterative Formulae:) Tj
T*
(   x = \(20 + 3y - 2z\) / 8) Tj
T*
(   y = \(33 - 4x + z\) / 11) Tj
T*
(   z = \(35 - 6x - 3y\) / 12) Tj
T*
(   3. Iteration Computations:) Tj
T*
(   Initial Guess: x^\(0\) = 0, y^\(0\) = 0, z^\(0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Iteration 1:) Tj
T*
(   x^\(1\) = \(20 + 0 - 0\) / 8 = 2.5000.) Tj
T*
(   y^\(1\) = \(33 - 4\(2.5000\) + 0\) / 11 = \(33 - 10\) / 11 = 23 / 11 = 2.0909.) Tj
T*
(   z^\(1\) = \(35 - 6\(2.5000\) - 3\(2.0909\)\) / 12 = \(35 - 15 - 6.2727\) / 12 = 13.7273 / 12 = 1.1439.) Tj
T*
(   - Iteration 2:) Tj
T*
(   x^\(2\) = \(20 + 3\(2.0909\) - 2\(1.1439\)\) / 8 = \(20 + 6.2727 - 2.2878\) / 8 = 23.9849 / 8 = 2.9981.) Tj
T*
(   y^\(2\) = \(33 - 4\(2.9981\) + 1.1439\) / 11 = \(33 - 11.9924 + 1.1439\) / 11 = 22.1515 / 11 = 2.0138.) Tj
T*
(   z^\(2\) = \(35 - 6\(2.9981\) - 3\(2.0138\)\) / 12 = \(35 - 17.9886 - 6.0414\) / 12 = 10.9700 / 12 =) Tj
T*
(   0.9142.) Tj
T*
(   - Iteration 3:) Tj
T*
(   x^\(3\) = \(20 + 3\(2.0138\) - 2\(0.9142\)\) / 8 = \(20 + 6.0414 - 1.8284\) / 8 = 24.2130 / 8 = 3.0266.) Tj
T*
(   y^\(3\) = \(33 - 4\(3.0266\) + 0.9142\) / 11 = \(33 - 12.1064 + 0.9142\) / 11 = 21.8078 / 11 = 1.9825.) Tj
T*
(   z^\(3\) = \(35 - 6\(3.0266\) - 3\(1.9825\)\) / 12 = \(35 - 18.1596 - 5.9475\) / 12 = 10.8929 / 12 =) Tj
T*
(   0.9077.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
