(>> Solution to Question 11:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Prove that for any real symmetric matrix A: \(i\) All its eigenvalues are strictly real, and \(ii\) Eigenvectors corresponding to distinct eigenvalues are mutually orthogonal.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Proof that Eigenvalues of Real Symmetric Matrix are Real:) Tj
T*
(   - Let A be a real symmetric matrix \(A in M_n\(R\) and A^T = A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Then A equals its conjugate transpose \(Hermitian\): A^* = \(A^bar\)^T = A^T = A.) Tj
T*
(   - Let lambda in C be an eigenvalue of A with non-zero eigenvector X in C^n:) Tj
T*
(   \(Eq. 1\) A * X = lambda * X.) Tj
T*
(   - Take the complex conjugate transpose \(*\) of both sides of Eq. 1:) Tj
T*
(   \(A * X\)^* = \(lambda * X\)^* => X^* * A^* = lambda_bar * X^*.) Tj
T*
(   - Since A^* = A:) Tj
T*
(   \(Eq. 2\) X^* * A = lambda_bar * X^*.) Tj
T*
(   - Post-multiply Eq. 2 by X:) Tj
T*
(   \(Eq. 3\) X^* * A * X = lambda_bar * \(X^* * X\).) Tj
T*
(   - Pre-multiply Eq. 1 by X^*:) Tj
T*
(   \(Eq. 4\) X^* * A * X = lambda * \(X^* * X\).) Tj
T*
(   - Equating Eq. 3 and Eq. 4:) Tj
T*
(   lambda * \(X^* * X\) = lambda_bar * \(X^* * X\) => \(lambda - lambda_bar\) * \(X^* * X\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Since X is a non-zero vector, X^* * X = sum_{i=1}^n |x_i|^2 > 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore, lambda - lambda_bar = 0 => lambda = lambda_bar.) Tj
T*
ET

