(   [Problem Statement]: Find all eigenvalues and corresponding normalized eigenvectors of the real symmetric matrix: A = [[3, -1, 1], [-1, 5, -1], [1, -1, 3]]. Verify that the eigenvectors are mutually orthogonal.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Characteristic Equation det\(A - lambda*I\) = 0:) Tj
T*
(   Expand characteristic polynomial: lambda^3 - S1*lambda^2 + S2*lambda - S3 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - S1 = Trace\(A\) = 3 + 5 + 3 = 11.) Tj
T*
(   - S2 = Sum of principal minors:) Tj
T*
(   M11 = det\([5 -1; -1 3]\) = 15 - 1 = 14.) Tj
T*
(   M22 = det\([3 1; 1 3]\) = 9 - 1 = 8.) Tj
T*
(   M33 = det\([3 -1; -1 5]\) = 15 - 1 = 14.) Tj
T*
(   S2 = 14 + 8 + 14 = 36.) Tj
T*
(   - S3 = det\(A\) = 3\(15 - 1\) - \(-1\)\(-3 - \(-1\)\) + 1\(1 - 5\) = 3\(14\) + 1\(-2\) + 1\(-4\) = 42 - 2 - 4 =) Tj
T*
(   36.) Tj
T*
(   Characteristic equation: lambda^3 - 11*lambda^2 + 36*lambda - 36 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Factoring: \(lambda - 2\) * \(lambda - 3\) * \(lambda - 6\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Eigenvalues: lambda1 = 2, lambda2 = 3, lambda3 = 6.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Eigenvector for lambda1 = 2:) Tj
T*
(   \(A - 2*I\)X = 0 => [ 1 -1 1; -1 3 -1; 1 -1 1 ][x1; x2; x3] = [0; 0; 0].) Tj
T*
(   From row 1: x1 - x2 + x3 = 0. From row 2: -x1 + 3*x2 - x3 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Adding rows: 2*x2 = 0 => x2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Then x1 + x3 = 0 => x1 = -x3. Let x3 = 1 => x1 = -1.) Tj
T*
(   X1 = [ -1, 0, 1 ]^T. Norm ||X1|| = sqrt\(1 + 0 + 1\) = sqrt\(2\).) Tj
T*
(   Normalized u1 = [ -1/sqrt\(2\), 0, 1/sqrt\(2\) ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Eigenvector for lambda2 = 3:) Tj
T*
(   \(A - 3*I\)X = 0 => [ 0 -1 1; -1 2 -1; 1 -1 0 ][x1; x2; x3] = [0; 0; 0].) Tj
T*
(   From row 1: -x2 + x3 = 0 => x2 = x3.) Tj
T*
(   From row 3: x1 - x2 = 0 => x1 = x2.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: x1 = x2 = x3 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   X2 = [ 1, 1, 1 ]^T. Norm ||X2|| = sqrt\(1 + 1 + 1\) = sqrt\(3\).) Tj
T*
(   Normalized u2 = [ 1/sqrt\(3\), 1/sqrt\(3\), 1/sqrt\(3\) ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Eigenvector for lambda3 = 6:) Tj
T*
(   \(A - 6*I\)X = 0 => [ -3 -1 1; -1 -1 -1; 1 -1 -3 ][x1; x2; x3] = [0; 0; 0].) Tj
T*
(   Using cross-multiplication on first two rows:) Tj
T*
ET

