(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the criteria for diagonalizability of a square matrix. Define modal matrix P and spectral matrix D, and show that A^k = P * D^k * P^-1.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Criteria for Diagonalizability:) Tj
T*
(   - An n x n matrix A is diagonalizable over field F if there exists an invertible matrix P such) Tj
T*
(   that:) Tj
T*
(   P^-1 * A * P = D, where D is a diagonal matrix.) Tj
T*
(   - Fundamental Theorem of Diagonalizability: Matrix A is diagonalizable if and only if A) Tj
T*
(   possesses n linearly independent eigenvectors.) Tj
T*
(   - Multiplicity Criterion: A is diagonalizable if and only if:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) The characteristic polynomial splits completely into linear factors over F.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) For every distinct eigenvalue lambda_i, its Geometric Multiplicity equals its Algebraic) Tj
T*
(   Multiplicity:) Tj
T*
(   GM\(lambda_i\) = dim\(Null\(A - lambda_i * I\)\) = AM\(lambda_i\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Construction of Modal Matrix P and Spectral Matrix D:) Tj
T*
(   - Let lambda_1, lambda_2, ..., lambda_n be eigenvalues of A, and let X_1, X_2, ..., X_n be n) Tj
T*
(   linearly independent eigenvectors such that A * X_i = lambda_i * X_i.) Tj
T*
(   - Form the Modal Matrix P whose columns are these eigenvectors:) Tj
T*
(   P = [ X_1 | X_2 | ... | X_n ].) Tj
T*
(   - Since {X1, ..., Xn} are linearly independent, det\(P\) != 0, so P^-1 exists.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute the product A * P:) Tj
T*
(   A * P = A * [ X_1 | X_2 | ... | X_n ] = [ A*X_1 | A*X_2 | ... | A*X_n ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ lambda_1*X_1 | lambda_2*X_2 | ... | lambda_n*X_n ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ X_1 | X_2 | ... | X_n ] * diag\(lambda_1, lambda_2, ..., lambda_n\)) Tj
T*
(   = P * D,) Tj
T*
(   where D = diag\(lambda_1, lambda_2, ..., lambda_n\) is the Spectral Matrix.) Tj
T*
(   - Pre-multiplying by P^-1 gives: P^-1 * A * P = D.) Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of A^k = P * D^k * P^-1:) Tj
T*
(   - From P^-1 * A * P = D, pre-multiply by P and post-multiply by P^-1: A = P * D * P^-1.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute A^2:) Tj
T*
(   A^2 = \(P * D * P^-1\) * \(P * D * P^-1\) = P * D * \(P^-1 * P\) * D * P^-1 = P * D * I * D * P^-1 =) Tj
T*
(   P * D^2 * P^-1.) Tj
T*
(   - By mathematical induction, assume A^m = P * D^m * P^-1:) Tj
T*
(   A^{m+1} = A^m * A = \(P * D^m * P^-1\) * \(P * D * P^-1\) = P * D^{m+1} * P^-1.) Tj
T*
(   - Since D is diagonal, D^k is computed trivially by raising diagonal elements to power k:) Tj
T*
(   D^k = diag\(lambda_1^k, lambda_2^k, ..., lambda_n^k\).) Tj
T*
(   - Hence, A^k = P * D^k * P^-1 for any positive integer k. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
