(   [Problem Statement]: Diagonalize the matrix A = [[1, 6, 1], [0, 2, 0], [0, 0, 3]] and compute A^5 using matrix diagonalization.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Eigenvalues of A:) Tj
T*
(   Since A is upper triangular, its eigenvalues are simply the diagonal entries:) Tj
T*
(   lambda1 = 1, lambda2 = 2, lambda3 = 3.) Tj
T*
(   Since all three eigenvalues are distinct, matrix A is guaranteed to be diagonalizable.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Find Eigenvectors:) Tj
T*
(   - For lambda1 = 1:) Tj
T*
(   \(A - 1*I\)X = 0 => [ 0 6 1; 0 1 0; 0 0 2 ][ x1; x2; x3 ] = [ 0; 0; 0 ].) Tj
T*
(   Row 3: 2*x3 = 0 => x3 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Row 2: 1*x2 = 0 => x2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Row 1: 0*x1 + 6\(0\) + 1\(0\) = 0 \(x1 is free\).) Tj
T*
(   Let x1 = 1 => X1 = [ 1, 0, 0 ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   - For lambda2 = 2:) Tj
T*
(   \(A - 2*I\)X = 0 => [ -1 6 1; 0 0 0; 0 0 1 ][ x1; x2; x3 ] = [ 0; 0; 0 ].) Tj
T*
(   Row 3: x3 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Row 1: -x1 + 6*x2 + 0 = 0 => x1 = 6*x2.) Tj
T*
(   Let x2 = 1 => x1 = 6.) Tj
T*
(   X2 = [ 6, 1, 0 ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   - For lambda3 = 3:) Tj
T*
(   \(A - 3*I\)X = 0 => [ -2 6 1; 0 -1 0; 0 0 0 ][ x1; x2; x3 ] = [ 0; 0; 0 ].) Tj
T*
(   Row 2: -x2 = 0 => x2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Row 1: -2*x1 + 6\(0\) + x3 = 0 => x3 = 2*x1.) Tj
T*
(   Let x1 = 1 => x3 = 2.) Tj
T*
(   X3 = [ 1, 0, 2 ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Construct Modal Matrix P and Inverse P^-1:) Tj
T*
(   P = [ 1 6 1 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 1 0 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 0 2 ]) Tj
T*
(   det\(P\) = 1 * \(1*2 - 0\) = 2.) Tj
T*
(   Adjoint of P:) Tj
T*
(   Cofactors:) Tj
T*
(   C11 = 2, C12 = 0, C13 = 0) Tj
T*
(   C21 = -12, C22 = 2, C23 = 0) Tj
T*
(   C31 = -1, C32 = 0, C33 = 1) Tj
T*
(   P^-1 = \(1/2\) * [ 2 -12 -1; 0 2 0; 0 0 1 ] = [ 1 -6 -0.5; 0 1 0; 0 0 0.5 ].) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Spectral Matrix D and D^5:) Tj
T*
(   D = diag\(1, 2, 3\)) Tj
T*
(   D^5 = diag\(1^5, 2^5, 3^5\) = diag\(1, 32, 243\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Compute A^5 = P * D^5 * P^-1:) Tj
T*
(   P * D^5 = [ 1 6 1; 0 1 0; 0 0 2 ] * [ 1 0 0; 0 32 0; 0 0 243 ] = [ 1, 192, 243; 0, 32, 0; 0, 0,) Tj
T*
(   486 ].) Tj
T*
(   Now multiply by P^-1:) Tj
T*
(   A^5 = [ 1, 192, 243; 0, 32, 0; 0, 0, 486 ] * [ 1 -6 -0.5; 0 1 0; 0 0 0.5 ]) Tj
T*
(   Row 1: [ 1*1 + 0 + 0, 1\(-6\) + 192\(1\) + 0, 1\(-0.5\) + 0 + 243\(0.5\) ] = [ 1, 186, 121 ]) Tj
T*
(   Row 2: [ 0, 32\(1\), 0 ] = [ 0, 32, 0 ]) Tj
T*
(   Row 3: [ 0, 0, 486\(0.5\) ] = [ 0, 0, 243 ]) Tj
T*
(   Final Result:) Tj
T*
(   A^5 = [ 1 186 121 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 32 0 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 0 243 ].) Tj
T*
