(   [Problem Statement]: Define an orthogonal matrix and an orthogonal transformation. Prove that orthogonal transformations preserve: \(i\) Vector lengths \(Euclidean norm\), and \(ii\) Inner products \(angles between vectors\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definitions:) Tj
T*
(   - A real square matrix Q in M_n\(R\) is called Orthogonal if:) Tj
T*
(   Q^T * Q = Q * Q^T = I_n.) Tj
T*
(   - This implies that Q^-1 = Q^T.) Tj
T*
(   - An Orthogonal Transformation is a linear map T: R^n -> R^n defined by T\(x\) = Q*x, where Q is) Tj
T*
(   an orthogonal matrix.) Tj
T*
(   2. Proof of Preservation of Inner Products:) Tj
T*
(   - Let x, y in R^n with standard Euclidean inner product <x, y> = x^T * y.) Tj
T*
(   - Under the transformation T, x -> Q*x and y -> Q*y.) Tj
T*
(   - The inner product of the transformed vectors is:) Tj
T*
(   <Q*x, Q*y> = \(Q*x\)^T * \(Q*y\)) Tj
T*
(   = \(x^T * Q^T\) * \(Q*y\)) Tj
T*
(   = x^T * \(Q^T * Q\) * y.) Tj
T*
(   - Since Q is orthogonal, Q^T * Q = I:) Tj
T*
(   <Q*x, Q*y> = x^T * I * y = x^T * y = <x, y>.) Tj
T*
(   - Thus, the inner product is strictly preserved: <T\(x\), T\(y\)> = <x, y>. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Proof of Preservation of Vector Lengths \(Norms\):) Tj
T*
(   - The Euclidean length \(norm\) of vector x is defined by ||x|| = sqrt\(<x, x>\) = sqrt\(x^T * x\).) Tj
T*
(   - Under orthogonal transformation:) Tj
T*
(   ||Q*x||^2 = <Q*x, Q*x> = \(Q*x\)^T * \(Q*x\) = x^T * \(Q^T * Q\) * x = x^T * x = ||x||^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Taking positive square roots:) Tj
T*
(   ||Q*x|| = ||x|| for all x in R^n.) Tj
T*
(   - Thus, lengths are invariant under orthogonal transformations \(isometry\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Preservation of Angles:) Tj
T*
(   - The angle theta between two non-zero vectors x and y is given by:) Tj
T*
(   cos\(theta\) = <x, y> / \(||x|| * ||y||\).) Tj
T*
(   - In the transformed space:) Tj
T*
(   cos\(theta'\) = <Q*x, Q*y> / \(||Q*x|| * ||Q*y||\) = <x, y> / \(||x|| * ||y||\) = cos\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   - Hence, theta' = theta; angles are completely preserved.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
