(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove the Spectral Decomposition Theorem for a real symmetric matrix A. Show how A can be written as a sum of rank-one projection matrices.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement of Spectral Decomposition Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Every real symmetric n x n matrix A can be decomposed as:) Tj
T*
(   A = sum_{i=1}^n lambda_i * u_i * u_i^T,) Tj
T*
(   where lambda_1, ..., lambda_n are the real eigenvalues of A, and {u_1, ..., u_n} is an) Tj
T*
(   orthonormal set of eigenvectors of A.) Tj
T*
(   Each term P_i = u_i * u_i^T is an orthogonal projection matrix of rank 1 satisfying:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) P_i^2 = P_i \(idempotent\),) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) P_i * P_j = O for i != j \(mutually orthogonal\),) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) sum_{i=1}^n P_i = I_n \(resolution of identity\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Since A is real symmetric, by the principal axes theorem, there exists an orthogonal matrix Q) Tj
T*
(   whose columns are the orthonormal eigenvectors u_i:) Tj
T*
(   Q = [ u_1 | u_2 | ... | u_n ], with Q^T * Q = I.) Tj
T*
(   - Q diagonalizes A: Q^T * A * Q = D = diag\(lambda_1, lambda_2, ..., lambda_n\).) Tj
T*
(   - Pre-multiply by Q and post-multiply by Q^T:) Tj
T*
(   A = Q * D * Q^T.) Tj
T*
ET

