(   [Problem Statement]: Define a quadratic form, its matrix representation, rank, index, signature, and classifications \(positive definite, negative definite, indefinite, semidefinite\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition and Matrix Representation:) Tj
T*
(   - A Quadratic Form Q in n real variables x = [x1, x2, ..., xn]^T is a homogeneous polynomial of) Tj
T*
(   second degree:) Tj
T*
(   Q\(x\) = sum_{i=1}^n sum_{j=1}^n a_ij * x_i * x_j = x^T * A * x,) Tj
T*
(   where A is an n x n real symmetric matrix \(A^T = A\) with:) Tj
T*
(   a_ii = coefficient of x_i^2, and a_ij = a_ji = \(1/2\) * \(coefficient of x_i * x_j\) for i != j.) Tj
T*
(   2. Invariants of a Quadratic Form:) Tj
T*
(   - By Sylvester's Law of Inertia, every quadratic form can be reduced to canonical form:) Tj
T*
(   Q\(y\) = lambda_1 * y1^2 + lambda_2 * y2^2 + ... + lambda_r * yr^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Rank \(r\): The total number of non-zero terms in the canonical form \(number of non-zero) Tj
T*
(   eigenvalues of A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Index \(p\): The total number of positive terms \(positive eigenvalues\) in the canonical form.) Tj
T*
(   - Signature \(s\): The difference between the number of positive and negative eigenvalues:) Tj
T*
(   s = p - \(r - p\) = 2p - r.) Tj
T*
(   3. Classifications of Quadratic Forms:) Tj
T*
(   - Positive Definite: Q\(x\) > 0 for all x != 0. Equivalent to: all eigenvalues lambda_i > 0, or) Tj
T*
(   all leading principal minors > 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Negative Definite: Q\(x\) < 0 for all x != 0. Equivalent to: all eigenvalues lambda_i < 0, or) Tj
T*
(   leading principal minors alternate: Delta_1 < 0, Delta_2 > 0, Delta_3 < 0, ...) Tj
T*
(   - Positive Semidefinite: Q\(x\) >= 0 for all x, and Q\(x\) = 0 for some non-zero x. Equivalent to:) Tj
T*
(   all eigenvalues lambda_i >= 0 with at least one eigenvalue equal to 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Negative Semidefinite: Q\(x\) <= 0 for all x, and Q\(x\) = 0 for some non-zero x. Equivalent to:) Tj
T*
(   all eigenvalues lambda_i <= 0 with at least one equal to 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Indefinite: Q\(x\) assumes both strictly positive and strictly negative values for different) Tj
T*
(   non-zero vectors x. Equivalent to: matrix A has both positive and negative eigenvalues.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
