(   A = [ -1 5 -1 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 1 -1 3 ]) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Find the Eigenvalues of A:) Tj
T*
(   det\(A - lambda*I\) = lambda^3 - S1*lambda^2 + S2*lambda - S3 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   S1 = Trace\(A\) = 3 + 5 + 3 = 11.) Tj
T*
(   S2 = Sum of principal minors = \(15 - 1\) + \(9 - 1\) + \(15 - 1\) = 14 + 8 + 14 = 36.) Tj
T*
(   S3 = det\(A\) = 3\(14\) - \(-1\)\(-3 - \(-1\)\) + 1\(1 - 5\) = 42 - 2 - 4 = 36.) Tj
T*
(   Equation: lambda^3 - 11*lambda^2 + 36*lambda - 36 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Factoring: \(lambda - 2\)\(lambda - 3\)\(lambda - 6\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Eigenvalues: lambda1 = 2, lambda2 = 3, lambda3 = 6.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Construct Normalized Eigenvectors:) Tj
T*
(   - For lambda1 = 2: u1 = [ -1/sqrt\(2\), 0, 1/sqrt\(2\) ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   - For lambda2 = 3: u2 = [ 1/sqrt\(3\), 1/sqrt\(3\), 1/sqrt\(3\) ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   - For lambda3 = 6: u3 = [ 1/sqrt\(6\), -2/sqrt\(6\), 1/sqrt\(6\) ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Orthogonal Transformation Matrix Q:) Tj
T*
(   Q = [ -1/sqrt\(2\) 1/sqrt\(3\) 1/sqrt\(6\) ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 1/sqrt\(3\) -2/sqrt\(6\) ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 1/sqrt\(2\) 1/sqrt\(3\) 1/sqrt\(6\) ]) Tj
T*
(   Transformation: X = Q * Y, where Y = [y1, y2, y3]^T.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Canonical Form:) Tj
T*
(   Q\(Y\) = Y^T * \(Q^T * A * Q\) * Y = Y^T * D * Y) Tj
T*
(   Q\(y1, y2, y3\) = 2*y1^2 + 3*y2^2 + 6*y3^2.) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Properties and Classification:) Tj
T*
(   - Rank \(r\) = 3 \(number of non-zero terms\).) Tj
T*
(   - Index \(p\) = 3 \(number of positive terms\).) Tj
T*
(   - Signature \(s\) = 2p - r = 2\(3\) - 3 = 3.) Tj
T*
(   - Nature: Since all eigenvalues \(2, 3, 6\) are strictly positive, the quadratic form is strictly) Tj
T*
(   POSITIVE DEFINITE.) Tj
T*
