/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove Sylvester's Criterion for positive definiteness of a real symmetric matrix.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement of Sylvester's Criterion:) Tj
T*
(   A real symmetric matrix A in M_n\(R\) is strictly Positive Definite \(x^T * A * x > 0 for all x !=) Tj
T*
(   0\) if and only if all its leading principal minors are strictly positive:) Tj
T*
(   Delta_k = det\(A_k\) > 0 for all k = 1, 2, ..., n,) Tj
T*
(   where A_k is the k x k submatrix obtained by deleting the last \(n - k\) rows and columns of A.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Proof:) Tj
T*
(   - Necessity \(=>\):) Tj
T*
(   Suppose A is positive definite.) Tj
T*
(   For any k in {1, 2, ..., n}, let y in R^k be a non-zero vector.) Tj
T*
(   Define x in R^n by padding y with \(n - k\) zeros: x = [y; 0].) Tj
T*
(   Then x != 0, so x^T * A * x > 0.) Tj
T*
(   Expanding: x^T * A * x = y^T * A_k * y > 0 for all y != 0.) Tj
T*
(   Thus, each leading principal submatrix A_k is positive definite.) Tj
T*
(   Since A_k is positive definite, all its eigenvalues are strictly positive.) Tj
T*
(   The determinant det\(A_k\) is the product of its eigenvalues; hence Delta_k = det\(A_k\) > 0 for) Tj
T*
(   all k = 1, ..., n.) Tj
T*
(   - Sufficiency \(<=\):) Tj
T*
(   We prove by induction on n that if Delta_k > 0 for all k = 1, ..., n, then A is positive) Tj
T*
(   definite.) Tj
T*
(   * Base Case \(n = 1\): A = [a11], Delta_1 = a11 > 0. For any non-zero x, x^T * A * x = a11 * x^2) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
