(   > 0. True.) Tj
T*
(   * Inductive Hypothesis: Assume true for matrices of order n - 1.) Tj
T*
(   Let A be an n x n matrix with Delta_k > 0 for k = 1, ..., n.) Tj
T*
(   By hypothesis, A_{n-1} is positive definite and invertible.) Tj
T*
(   Partition A as:) Tj
T*
(   A = [ A_{n-1} b ]) Tj
T*
(   [ b^T c ], where b in R^{n-1}, c in R.) Tj
T*
(   Perform block Gaussian elimination: Let S = c - b^T * \(A_{n-1}\)^-1 * b \(the Schur complement of) Tj
T*
(   A_{n-1}\).) Tj
T*
(   Determinant identity: det\(A\) = det\(A_{n-1}\) * S => Delta_n = Delta_{n-1} * S.) Tj
T*
(   Since Delta_n > 0 and Delta_{n-1} > 0, we must have S > 0.) Tj
T*
(   For any non-zero x = [u; v] in R^n:) Tj
T*
(   x^T * A * x = \(u + A_{n-1}^-1 * b * v\)^T * A_{n-1} * \(u + A_{n-1}^-1 * b * v\) + S * v^2.) Tj
T*
(   If v != 0, then S * v^2 > 0 and the first term is >= 0 \(since A_{n-1} is positive definite\), so) Tj
T*
(   x^T * A * x > 0.) Tj
T*
(   If v = 0, then u != 0, so x^T * A * x = u^T * A_{n-1} * u > 0.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore, x^T * A * x > 0 for all x != 0.) Tj
T*
(   Hence, A is strictly positive definite. \(Proved\).) Tj
