(   [Problem Statement]: Define a linear transformation T: V -> W. Define its Kernel and Range. Find the matrix representation of T: P2\(R\) -> P2\(R\) defined by T\(p\(x\)\) = p'\(x\) + p''\(x\) with respect to standard basis {1, x, x^2}.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definitions:) Tj
T*
(   - Let V and W be vector spaces over field F. A mapping T: V -> W is a Linear Transformation if:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) T\(u + v\) = T\(u\) + T\(v\) for all u, v in V.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) T\(c * u\) = c * T\(u\) for all c in F, u in V.) Tj
T*
(   - Kernel \(Null Space\): Ker\(T\) = { v in V : T\(v\) = 0 }. Subspace of V.) Tj
T*
(   - Range \(Image\): Im\(T\) = { T\(v\) : v in V }. Subspace of W.) Tj
T*
(   2. Matrix Representation of T: P2\(R\) -> P2\(R\):) Tj
T*
(   - Standard basis for P2\(R\): B = { v1, v2, v3 } = { 1, x, x^2 }.) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluate T on each basis polynomial:) Tj
T*
(   * For v1 = 1:) Tj
T*
(   p'\(x\) = 0, p''\(x\) = 0 => T\(1\) = 0 + 0 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Coordinate vector: [T\(1\)]_B = [ 0, 0, 0 ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   * For v2 = x:) Tj
T*
(   p'\(x\) = 1, p''\(x\) = 0 => T\(x\) = 1 + 0 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   Coordinate vector: [T\(x\)]_B = 1*\(1\) + 0*\(x\) + 0*\(x^2\) = [ 1, 0, 0 ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   * For v3 = x^2:) Tj
T*
(   p'\(x\) = 2x, p''\(x\) = 2 => T\(x^2\) = 2x + 2 = 2*\(1\) + 2*\(x\) + 0*\(x^2\).) Tj
T*
(   Coordinate vector: [T\(x^2\)]_B = [ 2, 2, 0 ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   3. Assemble the Matrix [T]_B:) Tj
T*
(   The columns of [T]_B are the coordinate vectors:) Tj
T*
(   [T]_B = [ [T\(v1\)]_B | [T\(v2\)]_B | [T\(v3\)]_B ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ 0 1 2 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 0 2 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 0 0 ].) Tj
T*
(   4. Properties of [T]_B:) Tj
T*
(   - Rank\([T]_B\) = 2 \(pivots in col 2 and col 3\).) Tj
T*
(   - Nullity\([T]_B\) = 3 - 2 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Basis for Ker\(T\): { 1 } \(constant polynomials\).) Tj
T*
(   - Basis for Im\(T\): { 1, 1 + x }.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

