(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove the Rank-Nullity Theorem \(Dimension Theorem\) for an arbitrary linear transformation T: V -> W between finite-dimensional vector spaces.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Formal Statement of Dimension Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Let V and W be vector spaces over field F, with V finite-dimensional.) Tj
T*
(   If T: V -> W is a linear transformation, then:) Tj
T*
(   dim\(V\) = dim\(Ker\(T\)\) + dim\(Im\(T\)\) = nullity\(T\) + rank\(T\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Complete Mathematical Proof:) Tj
T*
(   - Let dim\(V\) = n, and let nullity\(T\) = dim\(Ker\(T\)\) = k.) Tj
T*
(   - Since Ker\(T\) is a subspace of V, it possesses an ordered basis: { u1, u2, ..., uk }.) Tj
T*
(   - By the Basis Extension Theorem, any linearly independent set in a finite-dimensional space) Tj
T*
(   can be extended to a basis of the entire space.) Tj
T*
(   - Extend { u1, ..., uk } to a full basis of V:) Tj
T*
(   B = { u1, u2, ..., uk, v1, v2, ..., v_{n-k} }, where dim\(V\) = n.) Tj
T*
(   - We claim that the set S = { T\(v1\), T\(v2\), ..., T\(v_{n-k}\) } forms a basis for Im\(T\).) Tj
T*
(   - Part \(a\): S spans Im\(T\):) Tj
T*
(   Let w in Im\(T\). Then w = T\(v\) for some v in V.) Tj
T*
(   Express v in terms of the basis B:) Tj
T*
(   v = a1*u1 + ... + ak*uk + b1*v1 + ... + b_{n-k}*v_{n-k}.) Tj
T*
(   Apply linear transformation T:) Tj
T*
(   T\(v\) = a1*T\(u1\) + ... + ak*T\(uk\) + b1*T\(v1\) + ... + b_{n-k}*T\(v_{n-k}\).) Tj
T*
(   Since u_i in Ker\(T\), T\(u_i\) = 0 for all i = 1, ..., k.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: T\(v\) = b1*T\(v1\) + ... + b_{n-k}*T\(v_{n-k}\).) Tj
T*
(   Thus, w is a linear combination of S; S spans Im\(T\).) Tj
T*
(   - Part \(b\): S is linearly independent:) Tj
T*
(   Suppose c1*T\(v1\) + c2*T\(v2\) + ... + c_{n-k}*T\(v_{n-k}\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   By linearity of T:) Tj
T*
(   T\(c1*v1 + c2*v2 + ... + c_{n-k}*v_{n-k}\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   This implies that the vector z = \(c1*v1 + ... + c_{n-k}*v_{n-k}\) belongs to Ker\(T\).) Tj
T*
(   Since { u1, ..., uk } is a basis for Ker\(T\), z must be expressible as:) Tj
T*
(   c1*v1 + ... + c_{n-k}*v_{n-k} = d1*u1 + ... + dk*uk) Tj
T*
(   => d1*u1 + ... + dk*uk - c1*v1 - ... - c_{n-k}*v_{n-k} = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Since B is a basis for V, all basis vectors are linearly independent.) Tj
T*
(   Hence, all coefficients must vanish: d1 = ... = dk = c1 = ... = c_{n-k} = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Specifically, c1 = c2 = ... = c_{n-k} = 0.) Tj
T*
(   This proves that S is linearly independent.) Tj
T*
(   - Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   Since S spans Im\(T\) and is linearly independent, S is a basis for Im\(T\).) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: dim\(Im\(T\)\) = |S| = n - k.) Tj
T*
(   Adding: dim\(Ker\(T\)\) + dim\(Im\(T\)\) = k + \(n - k\) = n = dim\(V\). \(Hence proved\).) Tj
T*
