(   [Problem Statement]: Derive Cramer's Rule for solving a system of n linear equations in n unknowns. Solve the following 3x3 system using Cramer's rule: 2x - y + 3z = 9; x + y + z = 6; x - y + z = 2.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Derivation of Cramer's Rule:) Tj
T*
(   - Consider the linear system AX = B, where A is an n x n invertible matrix \(det\(A\) != 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Then X = A^-1 * B.) Tj
T*
(   - Using the adjoint formula: A^-1 = \(1 / det\(A\)\) * adj\(A\).) Tj
T*
(   - The j-th variable x_j is the j-th component of vector X:) Tj
T*
(   x_j = \(1 / det\(A\)\) * sum_{i=1}^n [adj\(A\)]_ji * b_i = \(1 / det\(A\)\) * sum_{i=1}^n C_ij * b_i,) Tj
T*
ET

