(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the mathematical theory of Singular Value Decomposition \(SVD\). Define singular values and express the pseudo-inverse \(Moore-Penrose inverse\) A^+ in terms of SVD.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Singular Value Decomposition \(SVD\) Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Let A be any real m x n matrix of rank r \(where r <= min\(m, n\)\).) Tj
T*
(   Then A can be factored as:) Tj
T*
(   A = U * Sigma * V^T,) Tj
T*
(   where:) Tj
T*
(   - U is an m x m orthogonal matrix whose columns u_i are the left singular vectors of A.) Tj
T*
(   - V is an n x n orthogonal matrix whose columns v_i are the right singular vectors of A.) Tj
T*
(   - Sigma is an m x n pseudo-diagonal matrix containing the singular values on its main diagonal:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma = [ diag\(sigma_1, sigma_2, ..., sigma_r\), 0; 0, 0 ],) Tj
T*
(   with sigma_1 >= sigma_2 >= ... >= sigma_r > 0.) Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of Singular Values:) Tj
T*
(   - Consider the n x n real symmetric positive semidefinite matrix A^T * A:) Tj
T*
(   \(A^T * A\)^T = A^T * \(A^T\)^T = A^T * A.) Tj
T*
(   - All eigenvalues of A^T * A are real and non-negative: lambda_1 >= lambda_2 >= ... >= lambda_n) Tj
T*
(   >= 0.) Tj
T*
(   - The singular values sigma_i of A are the non-negative square roots of the eigenvalues of A^T) Tj
T*
(   * A:) Tj
T*
(   sigma_i = sqrt\(lambda_i\(A^T * A\)\) for i = 1, 2, ..., r.) Tj
T*
(   - The right singular vectors v_i are the orthonormal eigenvectors of A^T * A:) Tj
T*
(   \(A^T * A\) * v_i = sigma_i^2 * v_i.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
