(   - The left singular vectors u_i are defined by:) Tj
T*
(   u_i = \(1 / sigma_i\) * A * v_i for i = 1, 2, ..., r.) Tj
T*
(   - These satisfy \(A * A^T\) * u_i = sigma_i^2 * u_i; hence u_i are orthonormal eigenvectors of A) Tj
T*
(   * A^T.) Tj
T*
(   3. Dyadic \(Rank-One\) Form of SVD:) Tj
T*
(   A = sum_{i=1}^r sigma_i * u_i * v_i^T.) Tj
T*
(   4. Moore-Penrose Pseudo-Inverse A^+:) Tj
T*
(   - If A is not square or singular, its Moore-Penrose pseudo-inverse A^+ is given by:) Tj
T*
(   A^+ = V * Sigma^+ * U^T,) Tj
T*
(   where Sigma^+ is an n x m matrix formed by taking the reciprocal of non-zero singular values:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma^+ = [ diag\(1/sigma_1, 1/sigma_2, ..., 1/sigma_r\), 0; 0, 0 ].) Tj
T*
(   - A^+ solves the general least-squares problem: for any AX = B, the minimum norm least-squares) Tj
T*
(   solution is X = A^+ * B.) Tj
