(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the Power Method algorithm for computing the dominant eigenvalue and eigenvector of a matrix. Apply the method for 4 iterations to matrix A = [[4, 1], [1, 3]] starting with initial vector X0 = [1, 0]^T.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Power Method Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   - Objective: Finds the eigenvalue of largest absolute magnitude \(dominant eigenvalue lambda_1\)) Tj
T*
(   and its corresponding eigenvector.) Tj
T*
(   - Assumption: Matrix A has a strictly dominant eigenvalue: |lambda_1| > |lambda_2| >= ... >=) Tj
T*
(   |lambda_n|.) Tj
T*
(   - Steps:) Tj
T*
(   1. Choose an arbitrary non-zero initial guess vector X^\(0\) \(not orthogonal to dominant) Tj
T*
(   eigenvector\).) Tj
T*
(   2. At step k, compute Y^\(k\) = A * X^\(k-1\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Normalize: let c_k be the entry of Y^\(k\) with maximum absolute value.) Tj
T*
(   4. Set X^\(k\) = \(1 / c_k\) * Y^\(k\).) Tj
T*
(   5. As k -> infinity, c_k -> lambda_1 and X^\(k\) -> dominant eigenvector X_1.) Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Computation for A = [[4, 1], [1, 3]] with X0 = [1, 0]^T:) Tj
T*
(   - Iteration 1:) Tj
T*
(   Y^\(1\) = A * X^\(0\) = [ 4 1; 1 3 ] * [ 1; 0 ] = [ 4; 1 ].) Tj
T*
(   Scale factor c1 = 4.) Tj
T*
(   X^\(1\) = [ 4/4; 1/4 ] = [ 1; 0.2500 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Iteration 2:) Tj
T*
(   Y^\(2\) = A * X^\(1\) = [ 4 1; 1 3 ] * [ 1; 0.2500 ] = [ 4\(1\) + 0.25; 1\(1\) + 3\(0.25\) ] = [ 4.2500;) Tj
T*
(   1.7500 ].) Tj
T*
(   Scale factor c2 = 4.2500.) Tj
T*
(   X^\(2\) = [ 4.25/4.25; 1.75/4.25 ] = [ 1.0000; 0.4118 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Iteration 3:) Tj
T*
(   Y^\(3\) = A * X^\(2\) = [ 4 1; 1 3 ] * [ 1.0000; 0.4118 ] = [ 4\(1\) + 0.4118; 1\(1\) + 3\(0.4118\) ] = [) Tj
T*
(   4.4118; 2.2354 ].) Tj
T*
(   Scale factor c3 = 4.4118.) Tj
T*
(   X^\(3\) = [ 4.4118/4.4118; 2.2354/4.4118 ] = [ 1.0000; 0.5067 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Iteration 4:) Tj
T*
(   Y^\(4\) = A * X^\(3\) = [ 4 1; 1 3 ] * [ 1.0000; 0.5067 ] = [ 4\(1\) + 0.5067; 1\(1\) + 3\(0.5067\) ] = [) Tj
T*
(   4.5067; 2.5201 ].) Tj
T*
(   Scale factor c4 = 4.5067.) Tj
T*
(   X^\(4\) = [ 4.5067/4.5067; 2.5201/4.5067 ] = [ 1.0000; 0.5592 ].) Tj
T*
(   3. Analytical Verification:) Tj
T*
(   - Characteristic equation: lambda^2 - 7*lambda + 11 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Exact dominant eigenvalue: lambda_1 = \(7 + sqrt\(49 - 44\)\) / 2 = \(7 + sqrt\(5\)\) / 2 = \(7 +) Tj
T*
ET

