12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the Leslie Matrix population model in biotechnology for age-structured microbial or animal cell cultures. Derive the characteristic equation for the intrinsic growth rate and explain the stable age distribution.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Formulation of Leslie Matrix Model:) Tj
T*
(   - In biotechnology cell harvesting and ecological fermentation modeling, a population is) Tj
T*
(   partitioned into m discrete age classes of duration Delta_t: x_k = [x_{1,k}, x_{2,k}, ...,) Tj
T*
(   x_{m,k}]^T at time t_k.) Tj
T*
(   - Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   * f_i >= 0: Fecundity \(birth rate\) of age class i.) Tj
T*
(   * s_i \(0 < s_i <= 1\): Survival probability of transitioning from age class i to i+1.) Tj
T*
(   - Dynamic System: x_{k+1} = L * x_k, where L is the m x m Leslie Matrix:) Tj
T*
(   [ f1 f2 f3 ... f_{m-1} f_m ]) Tj
T*
(   [ s1 0 0 ... 0 0 ]) Tj
T*
(   L = [ 0 s2 0 ... 0 0 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 0 s3 ... 0 0 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 0 0 ... s_{m-1} 0 ]) Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of Characteristic Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - Find det\(lambda*I - L\) = 0. Expanding along row 1:) Tj
T*
(   det\(lambda*I - L\) = lambda^m - f1*lambda^{m-1} - s1*f2*lambda^{m-2} - s1*s2*f3*lambda^{m-3} -) Tj
T*
(   ... - \(s1*s2...s_{m-1}\)*f_m = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Divide by lambda^m:) Tj
T*
(   1 = sum_{i=1}^m [ \(Product_{j=1}^{i-1} s_j\) * f_i * lambda^\(-i\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Define net maternity function phi\(lambda\) = sum_{i=1}^m l_i * f_i * lambda^\(-i\), where l_i =) Tj
T*
(   Product_{j=1}^{i-1} s_j is survivorship to age class i.) Tj
T*
(   - Since phi\(lambda\) is strictly monotonically decreasing for lambda > 0 with phi\(0+\) = infinity) Tj
T*
(   and phi\(infinity\) = 0, by the Intermediate Value Theorem, there exists a UNIQUE positive real) Tj
T*
(   root lambda_1 > 0.) Tj
T*
(   - By the Perron-Frobenius theorem for non-negative irreducible matrices, lambda_1 is the) Tj
T*
(   strictly dominant eigenvalue: lambda_1 > |lambda_j| for all j >= 2.) Tj
T*
(   3. Biological Implications and Stable Age Distribution:) Tj
T*
(   - Long-term population trajectory: x_k = L^k * x_0 ~ c * lambda_1^k * u_1.) Tj
T*
(   - If lambda_1 > 1: Culture grows exponentially with intrinsic growth rate r = ln\(lambda_1\) /) Tj
T*
(   Delta_t.) Tj
T*
(   - If lambda_1 = 1: Culture is stationary \(sustainable continuous bioprocess\).) Tj
T*
(   - If lambda_1 < 1: Population washes out \(extinction\).) Tj
T*
(   - Stable Age Distribution: The normalized right eigenvector u_1 corresponding to lambda_1 gives) Tj
T*
(   the invariant proportions of cells in each age class:) Tj
T*
(   u_{1,i} = \(l_i / lambda_1^{i-1}\) * u_{1,1}.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 29:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: In Metabolic Flux Analysis \(MFA\), explain how stoichiometric matrices and null space analysis are used to determine steady-state metabolic reaction rates. Illustrate with a simple 3-metabolite, 4-flux metabolic pathway.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Framework of Metabolic Flux Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Let a cellular metabolic network consist of m internal metabolites and n biochemical reaction) Tj
T*
(   fluxes v = [v1, v2, ..., vn]^T.) Tj
T*
(   - Dynamic mass balance for internal metabolite concentrations C:) Tj
T*
(   dC / dt = S * v - mu * C,) Tj
T*
