(   where S in M_{m x n}\(R\) is the stoichiometric matrix \(S_ij = stoichiometric coefficient of) Tj
T*
(   metabolite i in reaction j\), and mu is the cell growth dilution rate.) Tj
T*
(   - At metabolic quasi-steady state \(reaction rates are orders of magnitude faster than cell) Tj
T*
(   division rates\):) Tj
T*
(   dC / dt ~ 0 => S * v = 0.) Tj
T*
(   2. Null Space Analysis and Degrees of Freedom:) Tj
T*
(   - S * v = 0 is a homogeneous linear algebraic system.) Tj
T*
(   - The feasible flux distributions lie entirely in the Null Space of the stoichiometric matrix:) Tj
T*
(   v in Null\(S\) = Ker\(S\).) Tj
T*
(   - By Rank-Nullity Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Degrees of Freedom \(DOF\) = dim\(Null\(S\)\) = n - rank\(S\).) Tj
T*
(   - If DOF = 0: All fluxes are strictly uniquely determined.) Tj
T*
(   - If DOF > 0: The system is underdetermined. To determine internal intracellular fluxes,) Tj
T*
(   exactly DOF independent external flux measurements \(e.g., glucose uptake rate, oxygen) Tj
T*
(   consumption, lactate secretion\) must be supplied.) Tj
T*
(   3. Worked Illustrative Example:) Tj
T*
(   - Consider 3 metabolites \(A, B, C\) and 4 fluxes:) Tj
T*
(   R1: Substrate -> A \(v1\)) Tj
T*
(   R2: A -> B \(v2\)) Tj
T*
(   R3: A -> C \(v3\)) Tj
T*
(   R4: B + C -> Cell \(v4\)) Tj
T*
(   - Mass balances:) Tj
T*
(   For A: v1 - v2 - v3 = 0) Tj
T*
(   For B: v2 - v4 = 0) Tj
T*
(   For C: v3 - v4 = 0) Tj
T*
(   - Stoichiometric Matrix S:) Tj
T*
(   [ 1 -1 -1 0 ]) Tj
T*
(   S = [ 0 1 0 -1 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 0 1 -1 ]) Tj
T*
(   - Row reduction:) Tj
T*
(   Rank\(S\) = 3 \(3 independent rows\).) Tj
T*
(   Variables n = 4.) Tj
T*
(   Degrees of Freedom = 4 - 3 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Express fluxes in terms of free variable v4:) Tj
T*
(   From row 3: v3 = v4.) Tj
T*
(   From row 2: v2 = v4.) Tj
T*
(   From row 1: v1 = v2 + v3 = v4 + v4 = 2*v4.) Tj
T*
(   - General Solution Vector:) Tj
T*
(   v = [ v1, v2, v3, v4 ]^T = v4 * [ 2, 1, 1, 1 ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   - Biological Insight: Measuring a single external uptake flux v1 = 10 mmol/\(g*h\) immediately) Tj
T*
(   determines all intracellular rates: v4 = 5, v2 = 5, v3 = 5 mmol/\(g*h\).) Tj
T*
