(   [Problem Statement]: Model a multi-component bioprocess separation column using a linear system of differential equations dX/dt = A*X. Solve the system using the matrix exponential e^\(At\) where A = [[-2, 1], [0, -3]] and X\(0\) = [100, 50]^T.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Matrix Exponential Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   - For a linear autonomous dynamical system dX/dt = A * X with initial state X\(0\) = X0, the) Tj
T*
(   formal analytical solution is:) Tj
T*
(   X\(t\) = exp\(A * t\) * X0.) Tj
T*
(   - The matrix exponential exp\(A*t\) is defined by the convergent Taylor series:) Tj
T*
(   exp\(A * t\) = sum_{k=0}^infinity \(A^k * t^k\) / k! = I + A*t + \(A^2 * t^2\)/2! + ...) Tj
T*
(   - If A is diagonalizable \(A = P * D * P^-1\), then:) Tj
T*
