(   exp\(A * t\) = P * exp\(D * t\) * P^-1 = P * diag\(e^\(lambda_1*t\), ..., e^\(lambda_n*t\)\) * P^-1.) Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Solution for A = [[-2, 1], [0, -3]]:) Tj
T*
(   Step \(a\): Eigenvalues:) Tj
T*
(   Since A is upper triangular, its eigenvalues are the diagonal entries:) Tj
T*
(   lambda1 = -2, lambda2 = -3.) Tj
T*
(   Step \(b\): Eigenvectors:) Tj
T*
(   - For lambda1 = -2:) Tj
T*
(   \(A - \(-2\)*I\)X = 0 => [ 0 1; 0 -1 ][ x1; x2 ] = [ 0; 0 ] => x2 = 0, x1 free.) Tj
T*
(   X1 = [ 1, 0 ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   - For lambda2 = -3:) Tj
T*
(   \(A - \(-3\)*I\)X = 0 => [ 1 1; 0 0 ][ x1; x2 ] = [ 0; 0 ] => x1 + x2 = 0 => x1 = -x2.) Tj
T*
(   X2 = [ -1, 1 ]^T.) Tj
T*
(   Step \(c\): Modal Matrix P and Inverse P^-1:) Tj
T*
(   P = [ 1 -1 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 1 ]) Tj
T*
(   det\(P\) = 1.) Tj
T*
(   P^-1 = [ 1 1 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 1 ].) Tj
T*
(   Step \(d\): Compute exp\(A * t\):) Tj
T*
(   exp\(D * t\) = [ e^\(-2t\) 0 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 e^\(-3t\) ]) Tj
T*
(   exp\(A * t\) = P * exp\(D * t\) * P^-1) Tj
T*
(   = [ 1 -1 ] * [ e^\(-2t\) 0 ] * [ 1 1 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 1 ] [ 0 e^\(-3t\) ] [ 0 1 ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ e^\(-2t\) -e^\(-3t\) ] * [ 1 1 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 e^\(-3t\) ] [ 0 1 ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ e^\(-2t\) e^\(-2t\) - e^\(-3t\) ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 e^\(-3t\) ].) Tj
T*
(   Step \(e\): Apply Initial Conditions X\(0\) = [100, 50]^T:) Tj
T*
(   X\(t\) = exp\(A * t\) * X\(0\)) Tj
T*
(   = [ e^\(-2t\) e^\(-2t\) - e^\(-3t\) ] * [ 100 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 e^\(-3t\) ] [ 50 ]) Tj
T*
(   x1\(t\) = 100 * e^\(-2t\) + 50 * \(e^\(-2t\) - e^\(-3t\)\) = 150 * e^\(-2t\) - 50 * e^\(-3t\).) Tj
T*
(   x2\(t\) = 0 * 100 + 50 * e^\(-3t\) = 50 * e^\(-3t\).) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The concentrations of the two separating biotechnology components over time t are:) Tj
T*
(   x1\(t\) = 150*e^\(-2t\) - 50*e^\(-3t\)) Tj
T*
(   x2\(t\) = 50*e^\(-3t\).) Tj
T*
(   As t -> infinity, both concentrations decay stably to zero.) Tj
T*
